I have one more gripe with this, namely that if I am able to manually enable the chat while playing using <kbd>Tab</kbd>, I'd expect to be able to hide it back again with the same keybind. Especially so that sometimes it may be pressed because of a misclick.

The only option available to dismiss the focused textbox as-is seems to be to click away from it with the mouse. Otherwise it keeps collecting keyboard input (even the gameplay Z/X inputs).

Something like this seems to work like I'd expect it to:

```diff
diff --git a/osu.Game/Screens/OnlinePlay/Multiplayer/GameplayChatDisplay.cs b/osu.Game/Screens/OnlinePlay/Multiplayer/GameplayChatDisplay.cs
index 5d494379e6..c56c8eedd5 100644
--- a/osu.Game/Screens/OnlinePlay/Multiplayer/GameplayChatDisplay.cs
+++ b/osu.Game/Screens/OnlinePlay/Multiplayer/GameplayChatDisplay.cs
@@ -72,10 +72,19 @@ public bool OnPressed(GlobalAction action)
             switch (action)
             {
                 case GlobalAction.FocusChatInput:
-                    expandedFromTextboxFocus.Value = true;
+                    if (!expandedFromTextboxFocus.Value)
+                    {
+                        expandedFromTextboxFocus.Value = true;
+
+                        // schedule required to ensure the textbox has become present from above bindable update.
+                        Schedule(() => Textbox.TakeFocus());
+                    }
+                    else
+                    {
+                        expandedFromTextboxFocus.Value = false;
+                        GetContainingInputManager().ChangeFocus(null);
+                    }
 
-                    // schedule required to ensure the textbox has become present from above bindable update.
-                    Schedule(() => Textbox.TakeFocus());
                     return true;
             }
 ```
